  "caption": "Quinn texted while walking, met a kerb, and rolled an ankle. The plan: walk it off. It felt fine in a week — then rolled again two months later, and again after that.\n\nPain often settles before the ankle is truly ready. Balance and outer-ankle strength can stay low, and skipping rehab after the first sprain is linked with ongoing instability.\n\nWhat can help: move early with some protection, restore range and calf strength, train balance from a firm floor to wobbly surfaces, and earn your return to sport with hopping and side-step tests.\n\nGet it checked if you can't take four steps, there's bony tenderness, it may be a high sprain, or swelling is still there at six weeks.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
